Slight improvement in pulmonary edema and pleural effusions;
 however, persistent parenchymal opacities may represent either multifocal
 pneumonia or less likely ARDS.

New lingular consolidation.  This may represent pneumonia;
 however, in the setting of lung cancer, findings could be due to
